-Thank you.

00:01:16.175 --> 00:01:21.080
Thank you. Yeah, it's amazing.
I never expected it.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.982
You know, I auditioned
for the first "Thor" film

00:01:23.982 --> 00:01:26.552
ten years ago in 2009,

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:28.988
and I just thought I was
auditioning for a movie.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.157
You know, an interesting part
in an interesting movie.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:34.194
Back then, the Marvel Universe
was only --

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:35.929
They'd just made "Iron Man,"

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:39.399
and I thought,
"I'll, you know, have a go."

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:42.068
I didn't expect
to be casted at all.

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:44.737
So I can't believe I've got
my own show. So exciting.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:47.473
We go into production next year,

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:50.576
and, um, that's about as much
as I can tell you.

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:52.845
-Yeah, I was going to say. Yeah.
I know the way Marvel plays it.

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:54.414
You're not allowed to tell me
anything at all.

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.182
But you were telling me
backstage that when you

00:01:56.182 --> 00:02:00.186
auditioned for "Thor," you
actually auditioned for Thor.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.987
-I did. Yes, I did.

00:02:01.987 --> 00:02:06.259
Basically at the time,
they were, um --

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:10.296
They were looking for sort of
less well-established actors

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.731
so that the audience
didn't have an association.

00:02:12.731 --> 00:02:15.835
They just wanted people
to see these new characters,

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:17.403
these new actors.
-Yeah.

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.839
-And the remit was,

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:23.376
if you're over 6'0"
and you've got blond hair

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:26.445
and, you know, you can come
and have a pop at it.

00:02:26.445 --> 00:02:28.948
So I actually auditioned.
I never auditioned for Loki.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:31.217
I only ever auditioned for Thor,
which is nuts.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.852
-And how long did
the audition process --

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.821
-It was about three months.

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.189
-Wow. So you thought
for a second --

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:38.290
You go, "This is real.
I could be Thor."

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:42.027
-I -- For a second.
For a time. For a second, yeah.

00:02:42.027 --> 00:02:44.464
-We have friends over at Marvel

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:47.767
that sent us the original
audition footage of you.

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.168
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:53.239
This has never been shown.
This has never been shown!

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:55.374
This has never been released.
-Okay.

00:02:55.374 --> 00:02:58.811
-Here's Tom Hiddleston
auditioning for "Thor."

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:01.380
-And, remember.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:04.217
You chose this.

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:07.987
For...

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.656
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:11.857
-Come on!

00:03:11.857 --> 00:03:14.327
That's fantastic!

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:17.930
-Thank you very much.
You really are too kind.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:22.668
Um, I think we can all agree
that they cast the right actor.

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:25.471
-Let's talk about "Betrayal."

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.573
This is -- Only two weeks left
in this run.

00:03:27.573 --> 00:03:31.277
-Yes. Two weeks left.
We've done it over 200 times.

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:33.179
220, I think.
-Wow.

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:36.449
[ Cheers and applause ]
Fantastic.

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:39.652
-And so, yeah,
we close on December the 8th

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:42.021
at the Jacobs Theatre
on 45th Street.

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:44.056
-What is the story about?
Could we --

00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:45.124
-Yeah, loosely, yes.

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:47.493
I play a publisher
called Robert.

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:50.629
And married to Emma,
a gallerist.

00:03:50.629 --> 00:03:52.732
And there's my best friend,
Jerry,

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:55.000
who was best man at our wedding.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.037
And Jerry and Emma
have been having an affair.

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.605
[ Audience oohs ]

00:03:59.605 --> 00:04:01.407
-"Betrayal."

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:02.975
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.975 --> 00:04:05.911
-This is very sad,
and it's also very funny.

00:04:05.911 --> 00:04:08.581
And it's told in reverse order.
And it's --

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:11.083
My costars are Zawe Ashton
and Charlie Cox.

00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:13.586
And we've been doing this
for a year, and it has been --

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.888
It's a masterpiece. It's
Harold Pinter's masterpiece.

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:19.425
-I don't know how you --
I mean, you cry,

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:22.428
like, in this play,
and you do this every play?

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:25.097
Do you cry every --
-Eight shows a week. Yeah.

00:04:25.097 --> 00:04:28.968
We -- There's a --
I mean, it's called "Betrayal."

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.803
-Yes, I understand, yeah,
but, I mean, you --

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:34.006
I would be like...

00:04:34.006 --> 00:04:36.842
-Oh, no, no. I have seen --
I've seen you do your thing.

00:04:36.842 --> 00:04:38.310
-You've seen my --
-I have seen you.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:39.512
-You've seen me act?

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:41.581
-I think you're
a fine actor, yeah.

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:43.949
-You're seeing the wrong person.
Yeah, no, no.

00:04:43.949 --> 00:04:46.518
-I'm sure you could do it.
I'm sure you could.

00:04:46.518 --> 00:04:47.920
-Could you cry on command,

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.922
