-We're rooting for the world.

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:33.352
-We're rooting for the world,
always.

00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:34.787
-Absolutely, yes.
-But it was hilarious.

00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:37.657
I mean, in training we had --
we -- there was a --

00:07:37.657 --> 00:07:39.692
there was a moment where,
like -- 'cause I --

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:42.527
as I say, I'm keen,
maybe not entirely skillful,

00:07:42.527 --> 00:07:44.763
but I put in a bit
of a sort of hard challenge

00:07:44.763 --> 00:07:46.198
on my opposite number.

00:07:46.198 --> 00:07:48.200
And she was like, "Oh, ref,
did you see that challenge?"

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:49.434
And the ref was like,
"He's Loki.

00:07:49.434 --> 00:07:50.736
He's using his magical powers.
What can I do?"

00:07:50.736 --> 00:07:52.070
-Yeah, exactly.
Yeah, you can use that.

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:54.273
But I saw you running
with Usain Bolt.

00:07:54.273 --> 00:07:57.309
-Well, so, this is a kickoff.
I didn't -- I was playing right,

00:07:57.309 --> 00:07:59.311
